{{!-- The two shapes of "you cannot sign up here", each with the only honest action left.

	{{> "auth/shell" … card="auth/closed"}}

Invite-only means new memberships are closed and existing ones still work, so the action is sign
in. Members off entirely means there is nothing to sign into, so there is no action at all — and
in particular no Subscribe, because Ghost turns `@site.signup_url` into a feed-reader URL in that
state and a Subscribe button that means RSS is bait.

Both branches are reachable from a page a buyer left in their menu after turning memberships off,
which is exactly when a dead control does the most damage. --}}
{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
	<div class="text-center">
		<h2
			class="font-display tracking-heading text-2xl leading-[1.2] font-medium">{{t "Members only by invitation"}}</h2>

		<p class="text-small text-muted mx-auto mt-3.5 max-w-[38ch] leading-[1.65] text-pretty">
			{{~t "New memberships are closed. Existing members can still sign in."~}}
		</p>

		<a
			href="#/portal/signin"
			data-portal="signin"
			class="btn btn-primary font-ui mt-[26px] inline-block rounded-sm border px-5 py-[11px] text-sm font-semibold no-underline">{{t "Sign in"}}</a>
	</div>
{{else}}
	<div class="text-center">
		<h2
			class="font-display tracking-heading text-2xl leading-[1.2] font-medium">{{t "This publication does not have memberships."}}</h2>
	</div>
{{/if}}
